# House Price Prediction 🏠

## Project Overview
A Machine Learning model that predicts house prices
based on crime rate, rooms, location, and other 
features using the Boston Housing Dataset.

## Results 🎯
| Model | R2 Score |
|-------|----------|
| Linear Regression | 0.67 |
| Random Forest | 0.89 |

**Winner: Random Forest — 89% accurate!** 🏆

## Dataset 📊
- **Source:** Boston Housing Dataset
- **Total Houses:** 506
- **Features:** 13
- **Target:** House Price (medv)

## Features Used 📋
| Feature | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| crim | Crime rate |
| rm | Average rooms |
| age | House age |
| dis | Distance from office |
| tax | Tax rate |
| lstat | Low income population % |

## What I did 📝
- Loaded Boston Housing dataset
- Explored and cleaned data
- Trained Linear Regression model
- Trained Random Forest model
- Compared both models
- Predicted new house price — $21.7k!
- Analyzed feature importance

## Technologies Used 🛠️
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Scikit-learn

